---
interface Props { projectType?: 'all' | 'website' | 'automation' }
const { projectType = 'all' } = Astro.props;
const automationOnly = projectType === 'automation';
---

<section id="project-planning" class="section project-planning" aria-labelledby="planning-heading">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2 id="planning-heading">Timing & your part.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="planning-overview">
    <div>
      <h3>{automationOnly ? 'A schedule built around your workflow.' : 'Allow about 1–2 weeks for a small website.'}</h3>
      {automationOnly ? (
        <>
          <p>A small, clearly defined automation can fit a 1–2 week window. I confirm the estimate after reviewing your tools, sample data, and the connections involved.</p>
          <p>You try an early working version, then we refine it and check the agreed test cases before handover. More involved integrations or unusual cases can take longer.</p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>That’s from our agreed start date, once the scope, content, and access are ready. For a straightforward site, I aim to share a first draft within 1–2 business days of starting.</p>
          <p>The rest of the schedule allows for your feedback, the included revisions, final checks, and your approval to launch.</p>
          {projectType === 'all' && <p>For a small automation, 1–2 weeks can also be a starting point. I confirm the estimate after reviewing the workflow, tools, and sample data.</p>}
        </>
      )}
      <p class="schedule-note">This is a planning estimate. Some projects finish sooner; larger scope, missing materials, or slower feedback can extend the schedule. Before work begins, your quote confirms scope, revisions, price, payment terms, the start date, and target completion.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>A little preparation, a few review points.</h3>
      <p>Your main jobs are to explain the goal, gather the materials below, and review the work. Rough notes are fine for the first conversation; you don’t need a polished brief or technical knowledge.</p>
      <p>Plan for a short planning conversation, one collected feedback list per included revision round, and a final review.{projectType !== 'website' && ' For automation, that includes trying it with the agreed sample cases.'}</p>
      <p>I handle the build and guide you through what’s needed next. Timely replies help keep the agreed launch or handover date on track.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class:list={['preparation-grid', { 'single-project': projectType !== 'all' }]}>
    {projectType !== 'automation' && (
      <div class="preparation-card">
        <h3>For your website</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Your business details, services, audience, and what you want visitors to do.</li>
          <li>A few websites you like, with a note about what appeals to you.</li>
          <li>Draft text and any existing logo, brand colors, photos, or videos you want to use.</li>
          <li>Your current website address and any domain or hosting details you already have.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>No logo, photos, or finished copy yet? Tell me what’s missing so we can agree how to handle it and include any extra work in the quote.</p>
      </div>
    )}
    {projectType !== 'website' && (
      <div class="preparation-card">
        <h3>For your automation</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The task you repeat, the steps involved, how often it happens, and where it slows you down.</li>
          <li>The apps, spreadsheets, or systems you use and what needs to move between them.</li>
          <li>Sample inputs with private details removed, an example of the correct result, and any exceptions to handle.</li>
          <li>Who will use the result and who can arrange access to the relevant tools when needed.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A walkthrough or a few screenshots can help explain the process. We agree the required access and test cases during planning.</p>
      </div>
    )}
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .project-planning { scroll-margin-top: 115px; }
  .project-planning .section-heading { align-items: start; }
  .planning-overview, .preparation-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 32px; }
  .planning-overview h3, .preparation-card h3 { font-size: 1.3rem; }
  .planning-overview p, .preparation-card p, .preparation-card li { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .planning-overview p { margin-top: 14px; }
  .planning-overview .schedule-note { font-size: 13px; }
  .preparation-grid { margin-top: 32px; gap: 20px; }
  .preparation-card { padding: clamp(24px, 3vw, 32px); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 22px; background: var(--paper); }
  .preparation-card:first-child { background: #eef2dc; }
  .preparation-card ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 20px; margin: 18px 0; }
  .preparation-card li + li { margin-top: 10px; }
  .preparation-card p { font-size: 13px; }
  .single-project { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .single-project .preparation-card ul { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 14px 40px; }
  .single-project .preparation-card li + li { margin-top: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .planning-overview, .preparation-grid, .single-project .preparation-card ul { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
